      "role": "user",
      "content": "i know they aren't \"official\" codes, i'm not talking about some government thing, i'm talking about him. he was always so private and obsessed with detail, and he used to say that \"the truth is always in plain sight if you know where to look.\" it just feels too specific to be accidental. \n\nokay, let me try to explain. the first coin is a 1944-S. there's a dark oxidation spot right at the 4 o'clock position on the rim, almost touching the edge. the second coin is a 1945-D. there's a tiny bit of tarnish right under the 'D' mint mark, and it looks like a small vertical line. the third is a 1942-P, and there's a faint mark on the left side of Washington's hair. \n\ndoes the spacing or the positioning of those marks remind you of any kind of logical or mathematical progression? i'm trying to figure out if the oxidation is following a specific path.",
